{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"46c70cabb9f456961da6e3abb39c0c70711fc1c3b5135752bfbc61fe7322295c","packTokens":5811,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":173,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":981,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":4519,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's local SQLite database, with a few rows of sample data so each list has something to show\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Build the API side of the product with enforced business rules (capacity, waitlist, booking and cancellation windows, overlap, limit)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What should undo do to the stored booking, and what should it return on success?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Delete the booking row (as if it was never made) and return exactly the status and body that the contract declares for undoBooking\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When a Booked class has ended, does the booking become Attended? This affects the past list, 'classes this month' and the streak.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat it as Attended when read (derived, not stored)\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the /test simulate-other-member-cancellation hook be available in every environment?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Always map it, as the contract lists it\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Only the demo member exists, so how are other members' bookings and waitlist places represented, and how does promotion work when the demo member is not first in line (on cancel or simulate)?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Store other members as counts on the session (booked and waitlist). Promoting an anonymous first-in-line member lowers the waitlist count and moves the demo member's position up; the demo member is promoted only when they are first\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"The build runs Program.cs to write the OpenAPI document, and the code comment says nothing touches the database at startup. When and how should the SQLite schema and sample data be created?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Call EnsureCreated and seed at startup only when the database is empty, and skip this when the app is run to generate the OpenAPI document\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"After the member cancels a booking or leaves a waitlist, can they book or join the same class again? If so, does that create a new booking row?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Yes. Cancelled rows don't count for already_booked, and a new row is created\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should promotion notices (listed until acknowledged) be stored?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fields on the booking (promoted-at and notice-acknowledged)\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How much sample data should be seeded, and what dates should it use? The request says 'a few rows', but §4.3 asks for 40+ sessions over the current and next week, including full, almost-full and cancelled classes and the demo member's bookings.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Seed only a few rows (a handful of sessions plus the demo member's bookings), relative to the day the database is created\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The build shall generate an OpenAPI document at App.Api/openapi/built.json.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"The generated document shall contain the same 13 operationIds, paths, HTTP methods, parameters, request bodies, response status codes and component schemas as contracts/openapi.yaml.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The paths in the generated document shall be written as in the contract, without the /api prefix.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"The generated document's server url shall be /api.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"The generated document shall not include the existing GET / route.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"The GET / route shall keep answering \\\"API is up\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"The contents of contracts/openapi.yaml shall remain unedited by the build.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The API shall answer each of the 13 contract operations using the contract's declared HTTP method.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The API shall answer each of the 13 contract operations both at the /api-prefixed path and at the path as written in the contract.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me shall return status 200 with id 1, name \\\"Alex Rivera\\\", initials \\\"AR\\\" and membership \\\"Unlimited Monthly\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule shall return status 200 with today, date, weekStart, canGoPreviousWeek, canGoNextWeek, a list of 7 days, and the selected day's sessions, computed as described.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"canGoPreviousWeek shall be true only when the requested date is in the next week.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"canGoNextWeek shall be true only when the requested date is in the current week.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Each of the 7 returned days shall run Monday to Sunday, be labelled \\\"ddd d\\\", and include isToday and hasSessions flags.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"hasSessions shall be true when at least one session starts that day, ignoring filters.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"The selected day's sessions, including studio-cancelled ones, shall be ordered by startsAt ascending.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule shall return status 400 with Error code invalid_request when the date is malformed or outside the current and next Europe/London week, or when type, intensity or timeOfDay is not a contract enum value.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"GET /schedule shall filter the returned sessions to those matching at least one listed value of every supplied type, intensity or timeOfDay filter, ignoring filters not supplied.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Morning shall be defined as a Europe/London start before 12:00, Afternoon as 12:00 to 16:59, and Evening as 17:00 or later.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Every Session shall report bookedCount and waitlistCount including both the demo member and other members.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Every Session shall report a capacityLabel \\\"{spotsLeft} of {capacity} spots left\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Every Session shall report an availabilityLabel of \\\"Cancelled\\\" when studio-cancelled, \\\"Full · N on waitlist\\\" when full, \\\"1 spot left\\\" for 1 spot, \\\"Only N left\\\" for 2 or 3 spots, and \\\"N spots left\\\" for 4 or more spots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"A full Scheduled session's availabilityLabel shall be \\\"Full · {waitlistCount} on waitlist\\\", including \\\"Full · 0 on waitlist\\\" when nobody is waiting.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"The API shall derive each Session's actionState and myBookingId for the demo member according to the described precedence of studio-cancelled, booked, waitlisted, started, booking window, full, and bookable states.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"When the demo member holds a Booked or Waitlisted record for a studio-cancelled session, actionState shall be disabled with reason \\\"Cancelled by studio\\\", checked before the demo member's record state.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"GET /sessions/{sessionId} shall return status 200 with the full Session including instructor, whatToBring, counts, labels, actionState and myBookingId, or status 404 with Error code not_found when the session does not exist.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"Any request naming a nonexistent sessionId or bookingId shall return status 404 with Error code not_found.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings or POST /waitlist with a missing, malformed, or non-integer-sessionId body shall return status 400 with Error code invalid_request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings that passes every booking rule shall store a Booked record and return status 201 with a BookingChange containing the booking, the updated session, and a message \\\"You're booked for {name} · {ddd HH:mm}\\\" in Europe/London time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings shall return status 409 with Error code cancelled_by_studio, class_has_started, or outside_booking_window, checked in that order, for sessions that are studio-cancelled, started, more than 7 days away, or less than 15 minutes away, storing no record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings or POST /waitlist shall return status 409 with Error code already_booked when the demo member already holds a Booked or Waitlisted record for that session, storing no record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings shall return status 409 with Error code class_full and a refreshed session with actionState join_waitlist when the session is at capacity, storing no record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings shall return status 409 with Error code overlap and a message naming the conflicting class when the requested session's time overlaps a session the demo member is Booked for.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings shall return status 409 with Error code limit_reached and message \\\"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\\\" when the demo member already holds 10 Booked records for future sessions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo shall, within 5 seconds of the booking's createdAt, delete the booking and return status 200 with an UndoResult and message \\\"Booking undone — {name}\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo shall return status 409 with Error code undo_expired after 5 seconds, 409 invalid_booking_state when the record is not Booked, and 404 not_found for an unknown id.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel shall mark a Booked record, whose class has not started, as Cancelled with cancelledAt now and lateCancel true only when the class starts in under 2 hours, returning status 200 with a BookingChange whose message begins \\\"Booking cancelled — {name}\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel shall return status 409 with Error code class_has_started if the class has started, 409 invalid_booking_state if the record is not Booked, and 404 not_found for an unknown id.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"Cancelling a Booked record shall lower waitlistCount by 1 when waitlistCount is greater than 0, or lower bookedCount by 1 when waitlistCount is 0.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"POST /waitlist for a full session that passes the booking rules shall store a Waitlisted record with waitlistPosition equal to the previous waitlistCount + 1, and return status 201 with a BookingChange whose message is \\\"You're on the waitlist for {name} · {ddd HH:mm} — you're #{position}\\\" in Europe/London time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"POST /waitlist shall return status 409 with Error code cancelled_by_studio, class_has_started, outside_booking_window, or not_full, checked in that order after not_found and already_booked, storing no record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist shall, for a Waitlisted record whose class has not started, store it as Cancelled with lateCancel false, waitlistPosition null and cancelledAt now, lower the session's waitlistCount by 1, and return status 200 with a BookingChange whose message is \\\"You've left the waitlist for {name}\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist shall return status 409 with Error code class_has_started if the class has started, 409 invalid_booking_state if the record is not Waitlisted, and 404 not_found for an unknown id.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"POST /test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation shall promote the demo member to Booked when first on the waitlist, otherwise decrement waitlistCount and move the demo member's waitlist position up by 1 if the waitlist is not empty, otherwise decrement bookedCount, returning status 200 with a SimulationResult, or 404 not_found for an unknown session.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"When the demo member is promoted to Booked by the simulate hook, the booking shall record a promoted-at value so a promotion notice is listed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"When the simulate hook runs and the demo member holds a Waitlisted record on that session but is not first in line, the SimulationResult shall return that Waitlisted booking with its new waitlistPosition and list no promotion notice.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"When the demo member is promoted from a waitlist, the API shall set the booking to Booked even if it overlaps another Booked class or exceeds 10 upcoming Booked classes, with skipReason null.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/promotion-notices shall return status 200 with one notice per unacknowledged promoted booking, each with bookingId, sessionId, sessionName, startsAt and a message, without acknowledging them.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"POST /me/promotion-notices/acknowledge shall mark every current promotion notice as acknowledged and return status 204 with no body.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/bookings shall return status 200 with an upcoming list (Booked and Waitlisted records whose class has not ended, grouped by day) and a past list (Attended, Cancelled, and Cancelled-by-studio records, most recent first), each row carrying a badge, canChange and isLateIfCancelledNow.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"While a Booked record's class has ended, the API shall report it with status Attended, badge \\\"Attended\\\" and canChange false, while the stored row keeps status Booked.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"GET /me/stats shall return status 200 with upcoming (count of not-yet-started Booked records), classesThisMonth (count of Attended records in the current Europe/London month), and currentStreakWeeks (consecutive Monday-to-Sunday weeks with at least one Attended record, counted back from the current or previous week).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"If reading or writing the database fails or any other exception is unhandled, the API shall return status 500 with an Error body coded storage_failure and a plain-text message free of exception type names or stack trace lines.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"The API shall store sessions, instructors and the demo member's bookings in a local SQLite database (connection string App, default app.db), so changes survive a restart.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"On normal startup, the API shall create the schema with EnsureCreated and insert sample data only if the database has no tables or no data, leaving existing data unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"While the application runs to generate the OpenAPI document for the build, the API shall not create, open, migrate or seed the database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"The sample data seeding shall include sessions timed relative to the day of seeding, covering at least one session that day, one bookable or joinable session, one full session with a waitlist, and one studio-cancelled session, plus demo member bookings including at least one upcoming Booked record, one Waitlisted record, and one ended Booked record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"The sample data seeding shall create between 3 and 12 sessions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"The sample data seeding shall create at most 15 sessions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"The API shall read the current time for every time rule, label, \\\"today\\\", and seed date from the TimeProvider registered in dependency injection, defaulting to the system clock.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}